            </td>
            <td class="result-value" id="res-adhoc-2023">-</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class="result-label">Adhoc Relief 2024</span
              ><span class="result-subtext">25% of Revised Basic</span>
            </td>
            <td class="result-value" id="res-adhoc-2024">-</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class="result-label">Adhoc Relief 2026</span
              ><span class="result-subtext">7% of Revised Basic 2026</span>
            </td>
            <td class="result-value" id="res-adhoc-2026">-</td>
          </tr>
          <tr id="row-diff-2026">
            <td>
              <span class="result-label">Differential Allowance 2026</span
              ><span class="result-subtext">2% of 2022 Basic</span>
            </td>
            <td class="result-value" id="res-diff-2026">-</td>
          </tr>
        </table>

        <div class="summary-card card-blue">
          <span>Gross Monthly Salary:</span>
          <span id="res-gross-salary">Rs. 0</span>
        </div>

        <div class="section-title">2. Monthly Deductions</div>
        <table class="result-table">
          <tr>
            <td><span class="result-label">GP Fund Subscription</span></td>
            <td class="result-value" id="res-gpf">-</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="result-label">Benevolent Fund (BF)</span></td>
            <td class="result-value" id="res-bf">-</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="result-label">Group Insurance (GI)</span></td>
            <td class="result-value" id="res-gi">-</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="result-label">Income Tax (Estimated)</span></td>
            <td class="result-value" id="res-tax">-</td>
          </tr>
        </table>

        <div class="summary-card card-red">
          <span>Total Monthly Deductions:</span>
          <span id="res-total-deductions">Rs. 0</span>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-card card-dark-green" style="margin-top: 14px">
          <span>Estimated Net Salary (Take-Home):</span>
          <span id="res-net-salary">Rs. 0</span>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-card card-vibrant-green">
          <span style="font-weight: 600"
            >Net Increase in Monthly Salary 2026:</span
          >
          <span id="res-net-increase" style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800"
            >+ Rs. 0</span
          >
        </div>

        <div
          style="
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 11px;
            margin-top: 12px;
            text-align: center;
          "
        >
          *Note: Calculations strictly align with Sindh Finance Department
          Notification 2026-27 guidelines.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="info-section">
        <h3>How to Use the Sindh Government Salary Calculator?</h3>
        <p>
          Calculating your exact monthly salary is now easier than ever for
          educators across Sindh. Follow these simple steps to get your payslip
          details:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Step 1:</strong> Select your current Basic Pay Scale (BPS-01
            to BPS-22) from the dropdown menu[cite: 3].
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Step 2:</strong> Choose your current pay stage or
            increments[cite: 3].
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Step 3:</strong> Enter your current running basic pay
            according to the latest revised scales[cite: 3].
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Step 4:</strong> Click the "Calculate Complete Salary"
            button to view your gross pay, including medical, house rent, and
            conveyance allowances, along with any standard deductions[cite: 3].
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

